{title: 311 - I Would Be Like Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #311 • I WOULD BE LIKE JESUS • 15.14.14.13}
{lyricist: James Rowe}
{composer: B. D. Ackley}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 311}
{meta: tune I WOULD BE LIKE JESUS}
{meta: meter 15.14.14.13}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Earthly pleasures vainly call me; I would be like Jesus;
[G]Nothing worldly [D]shall [G/D]enthrall me; I would be like [D]Jesus.
[G/D]Be like Jesus, this my [D7]song, In the home and in the throng;
[Am]Be like Jesus, all day [G#m]long! I would be like [Am]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F#dim]Be like Jesus, [D/A]this my song,
[G]In the home [F#dim]and in [G]the throng;
[A]Be like Jesus, [D/A]all day long!
[D/A]I would be like Jesus.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]He has broken every fetter,
[G]I [D]would [G/D]be like Jesus;
[G/D]That my soul may [D7]serve Him better,
[Am]I would be [G#m]like Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]All the way from earth to glory,
[G]I [D]would [G/D]be like Jesus;
[G/D]Telling o'er and [D7]o'er the story,
[Am]I would be [G#m]like Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]That in Heaven He may meet me,
[G]I [D]would [G/D]be like Jesus;
[G/D]That His words 'Well [D7]done' may greet me,
[Am]I would be [G#m]like Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
